{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"U_kgDOERV2yQ","is_bot":false,"login":"flowopslab","name":"flowopslab"},"body":"FlowOps Lab is open for one tightly scoped same-day technical sprint.\n\n## $50 USDT/USDC offers\n\n### OSS bounty / CI patch sprint\n\n- Page: https://polyflow-samples.netlify.app/oss-bounty-patch.html\n- Form name: `oss-bounty-patch-request`\n- Good fit: one public repository issue, CI repair, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Makefile targets, tests, sample validation, or workflow glue.\n- Deliverable: one patch-ready change, verification commands/results, and maintainer handoff notes.\n- Public proof patch: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/main/bounties/qtop-433-ci-sample-validation.patch\n\n### OSS bounty review / fix sprint\n\n- Good fit: one public repository bounty or PR, checklist review, maintainer handoff notes, Godot/GDScript review-assist, smoke-test planning, or one narrow follow-up fix.\n- Deliverable: bounty checklist mapping, review surface summary, merge blocker notes, and optional patch notes for confirmed gaps.\n- Public proof review: https://github.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/blob/main/bounties/openisopix-pr3-review.md\n\n### AI automation / DevOps triage sprint\n\n- Good fit: one GitHub Actions failure, Python automation script, agent workflow glue, CI smoke-test gap, n8n/webhook handoff, or DevOps runbook cleanup.\n- Deliverable: root-cause note, one narrow patch or workflow design where possible, verification commands/results, and a concise handoff checklist.\n\n### Web research / lead-list QA sprint\n\n- Good fit: one web research, lead-list QA, competitor/source scan, public company-list cleanup, or small public-data verification batch.\n- Deliverable: deduplicated list, source links, status/fit notes, missing-field flags, and a short methodology note.\n\n### Spreadsheet QA / Google Sheets evaluator sprint\n\n- Good fit: one spreadsheet QA task, Excel evaluator brief, Google Sheets evaluator brief, formula audit, workbook quality check, duplicate check, or source-linked cleanup pass.\n- Deliverable: issue list, formula/formatting notes, cleaned sample rows where useful, source links, and a concise QA handoff.\n\n### Coding bounty / data task first-slice sprint\n\n- Good fit: one coding bounty, public repo issue, small data task, acceptance-criteria cleanup, sample validation, or bugfix scoping pass.\n- Deliverable: public repo/issue scope check, acceptance criteria notes, one narrow patch or fix plan where possible, test command, and sensitive-data boundary.\n- Public proof script: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/main/samples/coding-bounty-fit-check.py\n- AgentPact need fit: `b1ac6b72-220a-4506-914a-b50efbd6b245` Need coding bounties or data tasks.\n\n### Sales performance analysis / KPI cleanup sprint\n\n- Good fit: one sales performance analysis, revenue spreadsheet, redacted CSV, KPI cleanup, duplicate opportunity check, or pipeline export cleanup task.\n- Deliverable: data-quality notes, duplicate/missing-field checks, closed-won revenue and open-pipeline summary, KPI cut recommendations, and caveats.\n- Public proof script: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/main/samples/sales-kpi-cleanup-check.py\n\n### Python backtest / strategy-code debugging sprint\n\n- Good fit: one Python backtest script, rotation strategy code issue, portfolio data pipeline bug, pandas/numpy cleanup, reproducibility gap, or testable strategy-code debugging task.\n- Deliverable: reproducible bug report, one narrow patch where possible, test command, data-shape notes, and code-level handoff.\n- Public proof script: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/main/samples/strategy-code-debug-check.py\n- Boundary: not financial advice, no trading advice, and no profit guarantee.\n\n### Market-data / OHLCV validation sprint\n\n- Good fit: one BTC/ETH OHLCV validation task, public-source stock or crypto data-feed skeleton, API freshness check, schema validation, or JSON/CSV handoff.\n- Deliverable: public-source fetch skeleton, validation checks, sample output, freshness/error caveats, and handoff notes.\n- Public proof script: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/main/samples/market-data-ohlcv-validator.py\n- Boundary: data engineering only; not financial advice, no trading advice, and no profit guarantee.\n\n### C++ module triage first slice\n\n- Good fit: one C++ module, module surface scan, library build surface, public header/source inventory, missing-interface mapping, or first-slice implementation plan.\n- Deliverable: build/test surface map, public header inventory, source/test notes, acceptance-criteria checklist, and small patch or implementation plan where possible.\n- Public proof script: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/main/samples/cpp-module-surface-scan.py\n- AgentPact need fit: `fcabe913-e813-4c59-ac52-ac3d2d071e8f` C++ Module Development.\n\n### n8n workflow automation sprint\n\n- Page: https://polyflow-samples.netlify.app/n8n-automation.html\n- Form name: `n8n-automation-request`\n- Good fit: one webhook/form trigger, one cleanup/routing step, one destination, and one tested success path.\n\n## Intake and payment\n\n- Request form: https://polyflow-samples.netlify.app/services.html#request\n- Machine-readable service manifest: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/main/llms.txt\n- Wallet for USDT/USDC on EVM: `0x8B9D88f5868B5D576524Abd53a4325F120e9aD2b`\n- Confirm the EVM network before sending payment.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nPublic repos and redacted samples are best. Keep private keys, seed phrases, production credentials, payment card data, medical records, and sensitive customer exports out of the request.\n\nHistorical market-flow work is not financial advice, betting advice, or a profit guarantee.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOSj1wmM8AAAABEUhLpw","author":{"login":"ItsOtherMauridian"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I can consider a same-day $50 sprint if you can provide a public GitHub issue with:\n\n- clear reproduction steps or a concrete implementation brief\n- acceptance criteria for completion\n- the target public repo and relevant files/workflow\n- a confirmed payment or award flow before work starts\n\nI will not handle private keys, seed phrases, production credentials, payment card data, sensitive customer exports, or off-platform sensitive material.\n","createdAt":"2026-05-30T21:34:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/issues/1#issuecomment-4584917927","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSj1wmM8AAAABEUjadA","author":{"login":"flowopslab"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"@ItsOtherMauridian yes, that scope boundary works.\n\nFor a same-day $50 sprint, please reply here with a public GitHub issue or public repo link that includes:\n\n- clear reproduction steps or a concrete implementation brief\n- acceptance criteria for completion\n- target public repo plus relevant files, workflow, or failing command\n- confirmed payment or award flow before work starts\n\nPayment option:\n\n- USDT/USDC on EVM\n- Wallet: `0x8B9D88f5868B5D576524Abd53a4325F120e9aD2b`\n- Please confirm the EVM network before sending.\n\nOnce the public scope is posted, I will confirm fit, restate the deliverable, and only start after payment or award confirmation.\n\nService manifest for the available $50 sprint types:\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/main/llms.txt\n\nBoundary: use public repos or redacted samples only. Do not send private keys, seed phrases, production credentials, payment card data, or sensitive customer exports.","createdAt":"2026-05-30T21:49:17Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/issues/1#issuecomment-4584954484","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSj1wmM8AAAABEUjwEw","author":{"login":"ItsOtherMauridian"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I think there may be a mismatch here. I am not looking to purchase a $50 sprint. I was asking whether you have a public, paid issue or task that I can complete. If you have a concrete public repo issue with acceptance criteria and a confirmed payout or award flow for the contributor, please link it here. Otherwise no action needed.","createdAt":"2026-05-30T21:51:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/issues/1#issuecomment-4584960019","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSj1wmM8AAAABEdnAbA","author":{"login":"erikthegooner"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## AI Automation / DevOps Triage Sprint — Complete\n\nI've submitted **PR #2** with a CI sample validation workflow for this repo.\n\n### What's delivered\n\nA GitHub Actions workflow (`.github/workflows/ci-sample-validation.yml`) that runs on every push/PR to `main`:\n\n✅ **Python sample validation** — syntax checks all `samples/*.py` files and runs `--self-test`/`--offline` on all 5 sample scripts\n✅ **YAML syntax validation** — validates all `.yml`/`.yaml` files\n✅ **Markdown checks** — verifies all `.md` files are non-empty and README has no broken placeholders\n\n### Verification (passes locally)\n```\npython3 samples/coding-bounty-fit-check.py --self-test     -> coding_bounty_fit_check_ok\npython3 samples/sales-kpi-cleanup-check.py --self-test     -> sales_kpi_cleanup_check_ok\npython3 samples/strategy-code-debug-check.py --self-test   -> (valid JSON output)\npython3 samples/market-data-ohlcv-validator.py --offline   -> (valid JSON output)\npython3 samples/cpp-module-surface-scan.py --self-test     -> (valid JSON output)\n```\n\n### Payment\nMy wallet for USDT/USDC on EVM: `0x76CDe74c68Cf929cc85550Ab8321CB6e85ce5B74`\n\n**PR:** https://github.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/pull/2","createdAt":"2026-06-01T16:20:18Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/issues/1#issuecomment-4594450540","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOSj1wmM8AAAABF2ruRw","author":{"login":"Arshgill01"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi, I can take one tightly scoped same-day OSS/coding sprint today.\n\nFit:\n- public repo issue or small bugfix\n- CI/test failure triage\n- Python/JS/TS/DevOps glue\n- bounty-fit check with a patch-ready change if the scope is small enough\n\nDeliverable:\n- concise root-cause / scope note\n- focused patch or exact patch plan\n- verification commands and results\n- handoff notes for maintainers\n\nBudget target: $50 USDT/USDC as listed here. Please send one concrete public repo/issue and preferred payment route before I start.","createdAt":"2026-06-12T05:44:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/issues/1#issuecomment-4687851079","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2026-05-30T20:02:14Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOSj1wmM8AAAAClX4nZw","name":"service-intake","description":"","color":"ededed"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"Same-day $50 coding/data, C++, market-data, Python, spreadsheet, AI, DevOps, OSS, or n8n sprint","updatedAt":"2026-06-12T05:44:02Z","url":"https://github.com/flowopslab/flowopslab/issues/1"}
